                <span id="typesban"> </span>
                <span class="heading3">Our types of bananas</span>
                <br />
                <span class="questions">What types of bananas do you offer?</span>
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        At Peely we sell all types of bananas in every variation. From the smallest to the biggest to the most medium sized. We sell every banana you can imagine from all over the world. You can choose the banana that mostly resonates with you. The options are endless from our limited edition bananas to our regulars and customers' favourites you can choose freely. <br />
                        With even the ripeness of the bananas customizable, Peely gives you endless choices.
                        If there is something that you find missing do not hesitate to @Html.ActionLink("contact us!", "Contact", "Home", new { area = "" }, new { @class = "link-in-text" })<br />
                        The variation in our products always stays up to date and we offer all types of bananas that are currently popular on the market. With our amazing social media team, they constantly make sure that we give our customers the latest banana trends. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <br />
                <span class="questions">Do you sell different ripeness levels, like green, yellow, or overripe bananas?</span>
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        We know that finding the perfect banana is difficult. However, at Peely it has never been easier. We offer bananas in all different ripeness. If you would like your bananas at a specific ripeness there is a high chance Peely got it. <br />
                        We offer everything from green bananas to overripe bananas because we know that everyone prefers a different type. <br />
                        Our bananas are also perfect for baking. Sometimes when you bake you just need the perfectly ripe banana to enhance the flavours. Check out our @Html.ActionLink("product list", "Mproduct", "Home", new { area = "" }, new { @class = "link-in-text" }) to see exactly what type of ripeness levels we offer. <br />

                    </span>
                </div>
                <br />
                <span class="questions">What variety of bananas do you sell (e.g., Cavendish, Red bananas, Plantains)?</span>
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        Some types of bananas are quite rare. When you ask most people they have never heard of a blue java or Manzano banana. Whilst these might not be the most popular bananas they are still perfect in their own way. We do offer these special types of bananas on Peely.<br />
                        However, some of these are only available for a short period of time or in limited quantities. <br />
                        Although, we know this is not ideal. Some of these bananas are hard to come by at all times of the year. Sadly they aren't very popular either. Whilst we know this breaks our little bananas hearts it is the sad truth… <br />
                        That is why these special bananas are available throughout the year for a short period of time or in limited quantities. <br />
                        If you however would like any special type of bananas do not hesitate to @Html.ActionLink("contact us", "Contact", "Home", new { area = "" }, new { @class = "link-in-text" }) because we will do our best to deliver them to you.<br />
                        Nevertheless, throughout the year you can find the most popular banana types always available in different types and ripeness. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span class="questions">Do you offer plantains or other types of cooking bananas?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        As big baking enthusiasts, we offer all types of cooking bananas and bananas that are ready to be baked. We also offer recipes and already baked bananas like fried bananas. <br />
                        For new banana lovers it can be hard to navigate which banana is the best for the different baked goods. That is why at our @Html.ActionLink("recepies", "recepies", "Home", new { area = "" }, new { @class = "link-in-text" }) page you can find guidance in which bananas we recommend. <br />
                        Under our product list you can see all types of bananas and if you click on them you can find a little mark that shows if the specific banana is baking certified.<br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span id="quality"> </span>
                <span class="heading3">Quality assurance</span>
                <br />
                <span class="questions">How do you ensure the quality of bananas during transit?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        During shipping we know that plenty of things can go wrong. However, the quality of our products are our top priority. <br />
                        We ensure that all our bananas sustain their quality during transit in all organic ways. <br />
                        Our employees ensure that the temperature is controlled and kept at a level to help the bananas keep their freshness. We also make sure to manage the humidity and the ventilation to sustain the perfect conditions for our bananas. The bananas are regularly controlled by professionals during transit to make sure our products keep their high quality. <br />
                        If there would be any complications during transit we immediately contact our customers with the inconvenience and replace the product as soon as possible.<br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span class="questions">Is there a quality guarantee for your bananas?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        For all our products at Peely we guarantee top quality. With our customers being our number one priority we want to ensure 100% satisfaction every time. Every banana is put through a quality test before it leaves our farms. These tests have been structured so we test every aspect of the banana. Our specialist makes sure that the banana stays fresh not just in produce but also after transit. <br />
                        So when the banana reaches its destination it is just as fresh as before transportation. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span id="health"> </span>
                <span class="heading3">Health and nutrition</span>
                <br />
                <span class="questions">Are your bananas suitable for people with dietary restrictions (e.g., vegan, gluten-free)?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        Peely is about community and connection. Our main goal is that nobody feels left out or not seen on the banana market. Every banana needs a chance to live up to their full potential. <br />We make sure that our bananas match every single customer, even those with dietary restrictions. Specialists make sure that during produce and transit the bananas stay out of areas that risk infecting the bananas and become a danger to our customers.<br />
                        Everyone needs to get an equal chance to find their perfect banana… and every banana needs an equal chance to find their perfect owner. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span class="questions">Do bananas have any added preservatives or chemicals?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        The short but sweet answer to this question is no. All our products are 100% organic with no added chemicals or preservatives. <br />
                        At Peely we believe that a good banana can be achieved with care and with the correct circumstances. That is why we employ the best banana farmers who strive after perfecting our Peely farms around the world. With our scientist working day and night trying to find the best way to grow bananas without any chemicals we have achieved highly organic bananas for our customers.  <br />
                        We believe that a good banana should not contain any toxic preservatives or chemicals to be its best. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span class="questions">Are your bananas organic or non-GMO?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        Our bananas are organic. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span class="questions">Can I find information on the health benefits of different banana types?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        At our page we do not offer guidance on the different health benefits of bananas. We know however that this is inconvenient for our customers. That is why we are dedicated to fixing this issue in a short period of time. Currently our team is working on finding the best dietists and banana professionals to work together and put together a list with health benefits of the different bananas. <br />
                        Alas, this process might take a while and we deeply apologise for the inconvenience.<br />
                        Meanwhile we work on this feature, we recommend checking out <a href="https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/271157" class="link-in-text" target="_blank">MedicalNewsToday</a> for more information on health benefits.<br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span id="safe"> </span>
                <span class="heading3">Safety and handling</span>
                <br />
                <span class="questions">Are the bananas washed or treated before shipping?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        Before shipping all our bananas are treated with the same sincere care. They are carefully washed and treated with care before they are being packaged by professionals. These steps are carefully executed by our trained employees to maintain high quality. <br />
                        Our researchers worked hard to figure out the best way to treat our products before shipping it off to maintain its best quality when reached its destination. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span class="questions">Are there any allergens in the packaging or processing of your bananas?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        All our bananas are treated so that everyone can enjoy them. We avoid every type of allergen to make sure everyone who purchases a banana can freely enjoy it without worry. <br />
                        We know that it is a worry to make sure that everything you purchase is allergen free. <br />
                        That is why we have developed the safest system for everyone who lives with allergies. Our highly educated employees make sure that every banana is treated for in a way that those with allergies can enjoy fearlessly. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span class="questions">Are your bananas safe for babies or young children?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        Bananas are soft. Making it a great meal for the youngest. They are filled with great nutritious vitamins making them the perfect meal for children. <br />
                        Don’t worry about the tummy either! Bananas are easily digestible and may even help issues with the digestive system. They are a great source of energy to children due to their natural source of energy. <br />
                        Bananas are amazing for children and can be made into various meals. Just be careful. Whilst bananas are soft and easy to chew, cutting them into smaller pieces or even mash them makes it easier for children to eat them. <br />
                        No time to mash them? No worries! At Peely you can find already chopped and mashed bananas! And they are obviously baby certified. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span id="storage"> </span>
                <span class="heading3">Storage and freshness</span>
                <br />
                <span class="questions">Do you offer guidance on freezing bananas for smoothies or baking?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        At our @Html.ActionLink("recepies", "recepies", "home", new { area = "" }, new { @class = "link-in-text" }) Recipes page you can find all information on baking with bananas!
                    </span>
                </div>
                <span class="questions">Can bananas be refrigerated to extend their freshness?</span>
                <br />
                <div class="infotextbox">
                    <span class="infotext">
                        They absolutely can! If you store your bananas in the refrigerator it will slow the ripening process making them stay fresh longer. However, we wish they stayed fresh for a long time. Bananas can ripen and go bad in the refrigerator. <br />
                        If you decide to refrigerate your bananas make sure to bring them a coat! And keep in mind that there might be a bit of discoloration on the peel. <br />
                        If the bananas are already ripe the cold temperature may help it keep the inside fresh for longer. On the other hand, if the bananas aren't ripe enough the cold can interfere with the ripening process. <br />
                        Wrapping plastic wrap or foil on the stem of the bananas can slow the ripening process too. <br />
                    </span>
                </div>
            </div>
